- **"Derivative Work"** means any modification, fork, translation, adaptation, plugin, integration, or work based upon or incorporating any portion of the Software.
- **"Personal Non-Commercial Use"** means use of the Software by a single natural person ("Solo Individual") for personal knowledge management, private study, academic research, or unpaid educational evaluation, excluding any distribution for a fee, hosted service offering, or internal business operations of a for-profit legal entity.
- **"Commercial Use"** means any use of the Software or a Derivative Work that is not Personal Non-Commercial Use, including without limitation:
  (a) selling, leasing, sublicensing, or distributing the Software or any Derivative Work for direct or indirect compensation;
  (b) providing the Software or any Derivative Work as a hosted service, Software-as-a-Service (SaaS), managed platform, or API to third parties;
  (c) bundling, embedding, or integrating the Software into any commercial product, consulting deliverable, or paid course/service; or
  (d) internal deployment, evaluation beyond 14 days, or operational use by or on behalf of any for-profit corporation, partnership, startup, enterprise, or commercial team consisting of two (2) or more individuals.
- **"Gross Revenue"** means the total gross amounts invoiced, received, or accrued (before any deduction for taxes, hosting costs, salaries, marketing, refunds, or operating expenses) by a Commercial User and its affiliates from:
  (a) any product, service, subscription, or consulting engagement that incorporates, relies upon, or is facilitated by the Software or any Derivative Work; or
  (b) where the Software is used internally by a commercial entity without direct per-unit resale, the gross revenue of the business unit or product line utilizing the Software.

